- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` — entity field + validation
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/OwnerTelephone.java` — normalization helper
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/ValidateOwner.java` — validation/normalization step
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/CheckOwnerTelephoneUnique.java` — duplicate detection
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/ApplyOwner.java` — copies telephone onto entity (update path)
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/OwnerTelephoneInvalidException.java`
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/OwnerTelephoneInvalidExceptionHandler.java`
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/OwnerTelephoneDuplicateException.java`
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/OwnerTelephoneDuplicateExceptionHandler.java`
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/jdbc/JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl.java` — SQL columns (also JdbcPetRepositoryImpl, JdbcVisitRepositoryImpl reference it in joins)
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` — `OwnerFields.telephone` schema (source for the generated DTO)

OfficeFloor YAML:
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.OwnerTelephoneDuplicateException.yml`
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.OwnerTelephoneInvalidException.yml`

Tests:
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java`
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java`

## 2. Owner entity telephone field
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` (lines 47-51, getters/setters 78-84):
```java
@Column(name = "telephone")
@NotEmpty
@Digits(fraction = 0, integer = 10)
@Pattern(regexp = "^[0-9]{10}$", message = "Phone number must be exactly 10 digits")
private String telephone;
...
public String getTelephone() { return this.telephone; }
public void setTelephone(String telephone) { this.telephone = telephone; }
```
Note: the entity enforces **exactly 10 digits**, numeric only. `toString()` also includes telephone.

## 3. DTO classes
There are **no hand-written Owner DTOs**. The DTO is **generated** by the openapi-generator-maven-plugin into package `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto` with a `Dto` suffix (see pom.xml lines 385-388). So the class used throughout the pipeline is **`OwnerFieldsDto`** (plus `OwnerDto`), generated from the `OwnerFields`/`Owner` schemas in `openapi.yml`.

Schema in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` (lines 2026-2033):
```yaml
telephone:
  title: Telephone number
  description: The telephone number of the pet owner.
  type: string
  minLength: 1
  maxLength: 20
  pattern: '^[0-9]*$'
  example: '6085551023'
```
`telephone` is in the required list (line 2052). Note the DTO-level bean-validation pattern is `^[0-9]*$` with maxLength 20 (digits only, up to 20) — looser than the entity's exactly-10-digit rule.

## 4. Current validation / normalization logic
The authoritative runtime logic lives in the OfficeFloor functions (not the bean annotations).

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/OwnerTelephone.java` — single source of truth for normalization:
```java
/** Reduce a telephone to its digits; null becomes the empty string. */
public static String normalize(String value) {
    return value == null ? "" : value.replaceAll("\\D", "");
}
```

`/home/daniel/sandbox/.../owner/ValidateOwner.java` (lines 59-63) — strips non-digits and requires **exactly 10 digits**, then writes the normalized value back:
```java
String digits = OwnerTelephone.normalize(request.getTelephone());
if (digits.length() != 10) {
    throw new OwnerTelephoneInvalidException(request.getTelephone());
}
request.setTelephone(digits);
```
Blank-telephone check earlier (lines 53-55) adds "telephone" to the missing-fields list → `OwnerFieldsMissingException`. Invalid → 400 via `OwnerTelephoneInvalidExceptionHandler`.

There is **no E.164 / country-code logic currently** — it is a plain strip-to-digits + length-10 rule.

## 5. Duplicate-telephone detection
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/CheckOwnerTelephoneUnique.java`:
```java
public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerRepository ownerRepository)
        throws OwnerTelephoneDuplicateException {
    String telephone = request.getTelephone(); // already normalized by ValidateOwner
    for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
        if (telephone.equals(OwnerTelephone.normalize(existing.getTelephone()))) {
            throw new OwnerTelephoneDuplicateException(telephone);
        }
    }
}
```
Both sides normalized the same way; duplicate → 409 via `OwnerTelephoneDuplicateExceptionHandler`. This runs **only in the POST (create) pipeline**.

## 6. OfficeFloor YAML for owners create/update
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` — pipeline: `validate (ValidateOwner) → checkTelephone (CheckOwnerTelephoneUnique) → build (BuildOwner) → save → respond`.

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners/{ownerId}.PUT.yml` — pipeline: `validate (ValidateOwner) → load → apply (ApplyOwner) → save → respond`. Important: the **PUT/update path runs `ValidateOwner` (so it normalizes telephone) but does NOT run `CheckOwnerTelephoneUnique`** — no duplicate check on update.

Escalation mappings:
- `.../escalation/...OwnerTelephoneInvalidException.yml` → `OwnerTelephoneInvalidExceptionHandler`
- `.../escalation/...OwnerTelephoneDuplicateException.yml` → `OwnerTelephoneDuplicateExceptionHandler`

## 7. Existing tests
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/.../acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java` — these tests describe a **target E.164 behavior** (header comment: "telephone-e164: Telephone numbers must now be stored in E.164 form"), so they currently describe the desired/new behavior:
```java
@Test void coreNationalToE164() {               // "0412 345 678" -> "+61412345678"
    o.put("telephone", "0412 345 678"); int id = createOwnerOk(o);
    getOwner(id).andExpect(jsonPath("$.telephone").value("+61412345678"));
}
@Test void functionalityKeepsExplicitCountryCode() {  // "+64 21 123 456" -> "+6421123456"
    o.put("telephone", "+64 21 123 456"); ...
    getOwner(id).andExpect(jsonPath("$.telephone").value("+6421123456"));
}
@Test void errorRejectsUnformattable() {         // "12" -> 400
    o.put("telephone", "12"); createOwner(o).andExpect(status().isBadRequest());
}
```
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/.../acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java` — `uniqueTelephone()` (lines 98-104) generates a unique 10-digit AU mobile `04XXXXXXXX`; the doc comment explicitly discusses the 10-digit normalize rule and the `+61` E.164 / 9-national-digit expectation. `ownerNode()` (line 123) sets `telephone` via `uniqueTelephone()`. Tests hit only `POST /api/owners` and read back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`. (No duplicate-detection-specific test currently exists.)

## 8. Build system & phone library
- **Maven** (wrapper `/home/daniel/sandbox/mvnw`; `pom.xml` present, no Gradle). Spring Boot parent 4.1.0, artifact `spring-petclinic-rest` 4.0.2.
- Run tests: `./mvnw test` (JaCoCo configured; surefire via spring-boot-starter-test / webmvc-test). Full build: `./mvnw verify`. Note generated sources (OpenAPI DTOs via openapi-generator-maven-plugin 7.23.0, build-helper, MapStruct) are produced during the build, so tests depend on a generate/compile step.
- **No phone-number library is present.** `grep` for `libphonenumber`/`phonenumber`/`i18n` in `pom.xml` returns nothing. There is **no `com.googlecode.libphonenumber` dependency** — if E.164 parsing is needed it would have to be added. Relevant existing libs: MapStruct, officefloor-rest starter, openapi-generator, jackson (tools.jackson), jakarta validation.

